<title>UK: Rocco Forte signs contract for Russian hotel chain.</title>
<headline>Rocco Forte signs contract for Russian hotel chain.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sir Rocco Forte, who lost control of his Forte hotel empire last year to Granada Group Plc, has signed contracts to commence work on the first of a new chain of hotels to be set up throughout Russia.</p>
<p>The hotel, based in Nizhny Novgorod in central Russia, is owned by Spring Investments Ltd and will be managed by Forte's new group RF Hotels and their partners Commonwealth Properties Investors of the U.S.</p>
<p>A statement issued by Rocco Forte's office said talks were also underway to have the European Bank of Reconstruction and Development (EBRD) as an equity investor and a provider of debt.</p>
<p>The 150-bedroom hotel is expected start operations in 1998.</p>
<p>---London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
